  "derivation": {
    "v1_support": "green-max(red,blue)>=3 on exact canonical generated-family-v1 crop. Disk-radius2 closing with clamped coordinates, followed by3x3 box sum. w1_numerator is integer0..9; ID69 is forced9.",
    "v3_addition": "For six fringe tiles only: w3_positive=(accepted_v2 green-max(red,blue)<3) AND (generated_fringe green-max(red,blue)>2) AND (minimum tile-edge distance>3). For66/67/69 w3_positive=false.",
    "pure_sand": "(w1_numerator==0) AND NOT w3_positive. No final RGB equality or newly guessed grass segmentation selects a pixel.",
    "interior_proof": "Where w1=0, register_vegetation copies frozen47 exactly. register_interior requires old RGB != frozen47, so its weight is0 there. Therefore final remains frozen47 exactly when w3=0.",
    "clamped_border": "Dilation, erosion and box sum clamp coordinates independently at each selected192x224 tile, matching register_vegetation.cpp. V3 tile-edge uses local x%192 and y%224, matching register_footprint.cpp.",
    "rounding": "Pure backing selection is integer-only; does not approximate lround, infer alpha from output, or collapse staged rounded blends."
  },
  "invariants": [
    "Only RGB inside the one mask may change in a subsequent sand-only rebase. Keep source alpha255 and accepted RGBA outside the mask bit-identical.",
    "Accepted green RGB and full accepted green occupancy stay bit-identical. All mixed-transition pixels are protected.",
    "Do not freeze the entire four-HD-pixel tile border: its proven-pure-sand pixels belong to the writable domain, while its grass and transition pixels remain protected.",
    "Use new47 at identical local pixel coordinates, with no source crop offset or global phase shift.",
    "69 mask is all zero; its accepted PNG/HDA remain bit-identical. Include69 in all-nine family QA and existing builder/hash checks only.",
    "Original native source alpha occupancy is all opaque. Accepted green shape differs from original native green pixels; do not claim pixel-identical original grass geometry."
  ],
